    "title": "Liv Morgan Shares Injuries From 2026 WWE Royal Rumble - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Thomas Lowson ,\n51 minutes ago\nLiv Morgan is the winner of the 2026 Women’s Royal Rumble match, but the popular Superstar did not leave Riyadh, Saudi Arabia, unscathed.\nOn a recent edition of TMZ’s “Inside the Ring” podcast, Liv showed off her bruised hands, a setback from facing 29 other women last week. She said,\n“Do you guys see my knuckles? All my fingers are like bruised… This is just my battle wounds from the Rumble. You know how—seeing 29 other women? That’s insane.”\nREAD MORE: Celeste Bonin Loved Wrestling, But Has No Desire To Go Back\nREAD MORE: Ex-WWE Star Accused Of ‘Buying Views’ For His YouTube Channel\nHer hands aren’t the only things that are bruised, but Morgan made clear she’s feeling better after the difficult Rumble match. She said,\n“Yeah, I feel great now. I recovered. I feel fine now, but I was feeling it. You know, it’s a long, hard match. Lots of women, lots of, you know, flying legs and flying fists. It’s very chaotic. So I definitely have some bruises all over my body, but I’m feeling well today. I’m doing well.”\nMorgan, the #14 entrant, last eliminated Tiffany Stratton, who returned to the ring as the #30 entrant, to win the Women’s Royal Rumble match.\nMorgan is one of two women (alongside Nattie) to have competed in every Women’s Royal Rumble match. She will have a title match at WrestleMania 42.",
